WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.790
<b>BANDA TERRACE</b>

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:05.250
Let's go into town and search for demons today.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:08.000
Huh? But we already have a demon right here.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.830
Don't be silly. You said it yourself, didn't you?

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.920
That you would find a demon hiding in this town

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:15.580
and get clues from them
to help locate my sister, Sakura Chiyoda.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.210
Quit misusing the whatchamacallit rod.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.420
Ah, you took it!

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:19.880
Did you forget about all that?

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.000
I haven't forgotten! It's just...

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.500
I'm going to find another demon who lives in this city,

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.460
and hopefully through them get a lead
to find Ms. Sakura, because I owe her so much.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.580
It's only been a couple days
since summer vacation started,

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:35.830
but so much has happened that it feels like ages ago!

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.000
I agree. It feels like it's been a long time.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.290
I wonder why?

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:40.290
The time hath...

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.250
<b>The time hath...</b>

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.250
You're going to fulfill your promise, right?

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.250
Bring it on!

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.250
<b>Bring it on!</b>

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.210
I'll get it done!

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:45.250
<b>TA-DAAA</b>

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.040
Let's go start our search right now!

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.420
Sorry, there's one problem.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.210
Huh?

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.460
Unfortunately, we can't come with you this time.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.080
Why's that?

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:57.080
The demons in this town who knew my sister
are under the protection of a barrier.

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.630
So you won't be able to get close
if you have a magical girl with you.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:04.250
If you find one of the barriers,
just scope the place out and then come back.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:05.500
And be careful.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:08.540
You mean like the thing taped
to our front door? Roger that!

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.460
You're pretty gung-ho about this, Shamiko.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.580
I'm happy that Momo's asking me
to do something for once!

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.250
Because it means this is something only I can do!

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:15.960
Heh, heh, heh.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.040
<b>Heh</b>

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.040
<b>Heh</b>

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.040
<b>Heh</b>

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:20.130
Yep, it's all you. Pick up some ingredients
for dinner while you're at it.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:22.330
Enjoy being stuck here twiddling your thumbs!

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:23.330
Heh, heh, heh.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.630
Wise up, Shamiko! They're treating you like a stooge!

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:26.670
Heh, heh, heh.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:42.170
The excitement has just begun!

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:49.710
I have a feeling that a miracle will occur

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:56.960
A novice's skill is enough. Now, let's go!

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:59.920
It's all or nothing. We can go anywhere

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.630
Let me hear more even the sound of the core

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:09.420
If you and I put our hands together, there is nothing to fear

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.920
When I'm at a loss what to do,

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.170
I'll remember that you are here for me

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:17.920
You and I look up at the same sky

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.540
We smile at each other and overcome hardship too

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.960
Doing our best for someone

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:35.210
Isn't bad too

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:42.380
We are side by side again today

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:49.580
The excitement has just begun

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:02.040
<b>A NEW SPECIES DISCOVERED!</b>

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:02.040
<b>THE TOWN CAFÉ IS A DEMON LAIR!</b>

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:05.040
Choo-choo! Chugga-chugga, chugga-chugga!

00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:09.960
I think I got ahead of myself. Walking around randomly
and hoping for the best is gonna be tough.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.540
So what I'll do is...

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.330
You want me to tell you where demons hang out?

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.460
Well, I figured that you might know somebody...

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:20.710
Look, it's blazing hot out here
and you just popped in without any notice at all!

00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:25.670
Did you really think I could just conveniently whip up
some info for you on the spot like this?

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:26.750
Good point.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.250
I totally know a place where demons hang out.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.880
That figures, even you can't know everybody...

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:32.670
Wait, what?!

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.080
I know a spot where you can find demons anytime!

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:38.040
<b>CAFÉ</b>

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:38.040
<b>ASURA</b>

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:39.040
There's a café called Asura
down in the Tama Sakura shopping district.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:43.000
<b>CAFÉ</b>

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:43.000
<b>ASURA</b>

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.710
And the owner there is a demon!

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.880
Café Asura...

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:48.460
She was right. There's even one of those
barrier thingies hanging up.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:51.790
The owner packs a strong visual punch,
so try not to freak out when you meet 'em!

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.250
Well, I don't wanna spoil the surprise.
Go see for yourself!

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:57.500
<b>Ahahaha</b>

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.960
Exactly how strong of a punch is it...?

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:56.830
Gulp.

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.500
<b>GULP</b>

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.960
Maybe I can take a peek from outside...

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:03.920
Why hello there, Shamiko.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:06.290
Oh! It's you, Ogura...

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:11.420
<b>Part-time Help</b>

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:11.420
<b>Desperately Wanted!!</b>

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:10.000
Good afternoon! It seems like you've gotten
the hang of using a computer, huh?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.540
Huh? How did you know that...?

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:16.130
Do you wanna know a good site to visit?

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:19.920
I can welcome you to the underground. Sound good?

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.420
Uh, that's okay. No thanks!

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:26.540
All right! I've gotta get back to shopping,
so see you later! Bye!

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.750
Uh, bye! Stay safe!

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:30.880
Okay! Nothing's gonna happen if I stand here!

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:33.750
I just gotta step up and take the demon by the horns!

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:37.040
PARDON MEEEEEEEEEEE!

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.250
Huh?That's weird.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.000
Is there even anybody here?

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:45.710
Welcome in, hun.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.250
Now THAT'S a strong visual punch!

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.630
Oh boy, oh boy! You must be the owner!

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:54.630
'Fraid not.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:56.130
Does my look really pack a punch?

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.710
No. I'm sorry if I offended you.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.960
The café ain't open yet, but it's just about to be,
so make yourself at home.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.540
I can't imagine anybody
packing more of a punch than this.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:07.080
What the does the owner look like?!

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:13.710
Um, I'm actually not a customer! I saw the paper
hanging outside and need to talk to the owner about it!

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:16.130
Gotcha. I'll go and fetch 'im.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.580
Please and thank you.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.330
Packs a punch...

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:23.710
Well now, are you the little lady asking to see me?

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.080
Oh! Nice to meet you!

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:27.830
I'm the owner. My name's Shirosawa.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:28.880
NOW I SEE!

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.080
Go see for yourself!

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.670
<b>Strong punch</b>

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.330
A strong punch, huh...?

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.330
I know it must be a shock to see me like this.

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:39.040
Uh, no, it's just that...

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.710
I injured myself when asked to perform
a backflip the other day.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.000
They thought my athletic skills were "top-tier"...
But actually I'm just a "tapir."

00:05:45.290 --> 00:05:47.880
<b>JUST A TAPIR</b>

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.670
That's not the part I was shocked about!

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.750
You got it all wrong, Boss.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:53.420
It's those busted glasses you're wearing
that've thrown her for a loop.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.630
Huh? Really?

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:55.880
<b>BLUSH</b>

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:55.710
That's not it, either!

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:59.290
Hold the phone! I just noticed
some big clods growin' out of her!

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:00.750
You're right! That's bizarre!

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:02.080
Huh?! Look who's talking!

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.460
S-so, actually...

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.080
You don't have to say anything. I already know.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:11.000
This is the final destination where rebellious spirits
who are sent adrift always end up.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.080
The only demonic domain remaining,
nestled in a gap in a far East island nation.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:19.880
I've been waiting for demons
such as yourself to arrive here.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:23.960
Oh wow. Does this person, or uh,
animal really know everything?

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:24.000
<b>Person?</b>

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:26.210
You came to apply for the part-time job, right?

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:27.040
No, I didn't!

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:27.630
Huh?!

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:29.710
<b>PART-TIME HELP</b>

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:29.710
<b>DESPERATELY WANTED!!</b>

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:29.710
<b>Need to be available on weekends and holidays</b>

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:29.710
<b>Need to have proper and respectful manners</b>

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.710
I thought you came in
because you saw the paper outside!

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:31.540
That's not the paper I was talking about!

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:34.790
Well, we're hiring someone to work at the café, you see.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.170
My injuries have left me crippled and weak,

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:40.670
plus Lico has her hands full taking
the orders and serving everything on her own.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.750
I'm very sorry for the mix up.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.540
But I came here to ask you something else...

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:47.960
No, don't apologize.
Are you free on weekends and holidays?

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:51.460
Huh? I suppose I would be,
but I'm not sure why you're asking.

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.630
What about Christmas? Golden Week? New Years?

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:57.250
Are you the type who will come to work with a smile,
even on very short notice?

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.170
What?!

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:59.420
Lico! Make sure she can't escape!

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:03.130
<b>Tape her!</b>

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:03.130
<b>Tape her!</b>

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:01.830
Suspect in custody as of 9:45!

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:02.960
What the-?!

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:04.580
In custody!

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:07.040
I'm begging you! Please work here!

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:09.540
Our café is suffering a historic low in human resources!

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:11.460
Okay, but that's not why I came here!

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:12.580
GROVEL!

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:12.630
<b>GROVEL!</b>

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:16.500
Just give it a try! Let's say half a day!
No, three days! Or maybe even two or three years!

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:17.170
Huh?!

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:21.330
You're probably the first being in human history
to witness a tapir grovel on the ground like this!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.250
Say boss, if you're fit enough to grovel,
aren't you fit enough to work?

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.420
P-please pick yourself up off the floor!

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:28.880
Lico just doesn't know how to take a hint
and always upsets our customers!

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.460
I need an employee who knows how to be respectful!

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:33.170
Wh-whaat...?!

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:38.630
We open in 3 minutes, hun.
Here are all the table numbers.

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:40.000
Just this one time.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.080
I'm Lico.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:42.500
Your job is simple.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:46.500
Write the orders on this sheet here.
Then serve 'em, and clean 'em up.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:47.420
That's it.

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:48.130
Talk about a crash course!

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:51.380
This place is pretty small,
so I can handle working for a day!

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:54.080
I'll ask them about Ms. Sakura right away
once it slows down!

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:55.670
Yuko, hun! Got a party of two here.

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:56.580
Uh, okay!

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:57.670
Party of four.

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:58.330
On it!

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.420
Party of two, party of five.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:00.130
On it!

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:05.750
Party of one, one, four, five, and twelve,
plus 4 little kids and one pupper.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:04.830
On it! On it! Uh, on it!

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.880
How the heck do you get this much business?!

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.500
Well, it has to do with Lico being a Huli jing.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:14.790
<b>HULI JING</b>

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:13.040
The food that she makes is strangely addictive.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:15.290
Which means we constantly have customers
who never stop coming.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:17.580
That sounds like it could be illegal or something!

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:19.580
I have a lot of fun cooking.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:21.580
But I don't care a fig 'bout anything else.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:24.210
I'm thrilled to have you as part of the team, Yuko.

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:26.580
If I'm not careful, I really will end up working here!

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:29.330
I gotta hurry and get the info that I came for
and then get outta here!

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:31.830
Gotta get the info! Gotta get the info!

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:34.500
Gotta take the orders! Gotta get the info!

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:38.330
Gotta take the orders! Lunch Set A... Omlette rice...

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:41.330
Table 5! Order for Lunch Set B and curry!

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:44.710
The demon girl evolved into a waitress!

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.580
Yuko, hun. The lunch rush is over.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.790
Feel free to have a meal on the house.

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:51.630
Thanks for the food!

00:08:56.790 --> 00:08:59.670
Oh! Th-this is super yummy!

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:01.920
It feels like the core of my brain is unraveling!

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:06.460
Despite the fact I came here to fulfill an unpleasant
and important errand, it's evaporating into nothing!

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:11.500
Well, my dear, that's because you helped round
this dish off with the ultimate seasoning: manual labor.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:16.080
And just so you know, Yuko, all employees here...
can eat as much as they want for absolutely free.

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:26.250
Shamiko sure is late. I'm totally starving.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.330
<b>WELCOME TO THE FEUDAL</b>

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.330
<b>ERA OF CUTENESS</b>

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:30.460
I guess I'll grab something from the convenience store,
since we're done with our strategy session.

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:30.330
<b>EVERYONE IS HERE:</b>

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:30.330
<b>101 MASCOT CHARACTERS!</b>

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:30.330
<b>In theaters this summer</b>

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:31.210
<b>GRUMBLE</b>

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:31.670
Grumble...

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.420
Just wait. Have faith in Shamiko.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:36.380
She's the type who comes through despite everything.

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:41.960
<b>GRUMBLE</b>

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:36.790
Grumble...

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:41.880
I just know she's going to come through that door
with both useful information and yummy food for us.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:43.080
<b>GRUMBLE</b>

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:45.000
You're right! We already had convenience
store food for lunch, anyway!

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:49.460
Grumble... Grumble... Grumble...

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:45.000
<b>GRUMBLE</b>

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:46.420
The time hath...

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:46.920
<b>GRUMBLE</b>

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:49.460
Uh oh, these two are depending
on Shamiko for their essentials!

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:49.040
<b>GRUMBLE</b>

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:52.250
Hey everybody! I just got back!

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:54.170
Welcome back. How did it go, Shamiko?
Grumble...<b></b>

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:54.380
<b>GRUMBLE</b>

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:56.880
Momo! I found a part-time job!

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:57.380
Huh?

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:59.500
And I learned something very important!

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:02.460
Manual labor is... the ultimate seasoning!

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:05.130
Uh... huh.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:11.420
Don't give up, Shamiko! Learn about the value
of manual labor and enjoy even tastier food!

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.670
Is it just me or are you forgetting something important...?

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.670
Grumble...

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:14.920
<b>GRUMBLE</b>

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:28.630
Now for a quick recap.

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:33.670
Shamiko found a café that's staffed by demons
who may be able to provide some clues!

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:37.000
<b>BANDA TERRACE</b>

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:36.040
Let's have dinner!

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:49.170
<b>WHOA</b>

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:46.210
These are Yuko's spoils of war!
Whoa!<b></b>

00:10:46.210 --> 00:10:47.460
They're yummy!

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:49.130
You're amazing, Sis!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.000
Let's all dig in!

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.250
Fancy... fancy...

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:54.170
Huh? Why are you just staring at it intently, Seiko?

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:58.380
Because we can't dine upon food as fancy
as this without showing plenty of appreciation first!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:00.040
Staaaaare...

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:01.080
It'll get cold.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:04.130
All right, let me plate it so that it's easier to eat!

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:07.540
I'm gonna make it look like
the set meals we have at the café!

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:11.290
It's just like this!

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:12.880
Now it looks even more fancy!

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:16.040
Oh! I've seen something like this before
at our school's 6th grade lunch buffet!

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:18.080
<b>FANCY</b>

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:17.960
Looks good enough to go viral.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:21.960
<b>MWAHAHA</b>

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:21.830
Jobs in the food biz come
with nice perks, huh, Shamiko?

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:25.330
<b>MUNCH</b>

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:25.330
<b>FOO</b>

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:25.330
<b>MUNCH</b>

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:25.330
<b>FOO</b>

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:25.330
Eating with everybody makes it so yummy
that I just can't get enough!
Munch, munch... Foo, foo...<b></b>

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:30.460
You're right! We should share the blessing
of this delicious food with our neighbors as well!

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:31.960
Yeah! I thought so, too!

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:41.420
<b>FANCY</b>

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:35.960
That's why I delievered some large bread loaves
to Momo and Mikan earlier!

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.710
That's wonderful, Yuko!

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:41.330
I'm gonna make sure our family's first fancy dinner
goes down in the history books!

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:57.380
<b>BANDA TERRACE</b>

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:43.380
Aren't you going to eat some, Ryo?

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:45.920
I'll start eating after I get another shot from this angle.

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:50.920
Momo! This marmelade I have is perfect to go
with the bread that Shamiko gave us! How lucky!

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.420
No thanks, I'm just going to eat it plain.

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:56.130
What?! But it's way more delicious
when you put the marmelade on it!

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:57.380
I'm good. Seriously.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:05.630
Shamiko's been acting a teeny bit weird ever since
she started working part-time at that demon café.

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:10.080
Today they taught me how to slice sandwiches like a pro!

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.630
And I got to take home a lot of leftovers!

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:13.670
That wasn't the plan!

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:15.790
Just feast your eyes on these sandwiches!

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:18.250
Oh, yeah, they do look tasty...

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:21.000
You need to remember your mission, Shamiko!

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:23.330
Getting info from the demons that you found!

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:26.210
Oh, that's right. I totally spaced.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:28.210
I'll ask them about it tomorrow.

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:34.670
I'm off to work!

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:36.630
Have a good day.

00:12:36.830 --> 00:12:38.040
What do you think, Mikan?

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:39.540
Something is clearly off.

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:43.500
I can't believe Shamiko's learned how to prepare
café food that looks so high-class.

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:45.750
It feels wrong eating it in our tacky tatami rooms.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:47.540
Okay, yeah, but that's not what I meant.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:51.170
She's totally forgotten about her mission
for 4 days in a row.

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:55.080
For the first 2 days, it wasn't hard to believe
that's something Shamiko would do...

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:59.420
but her forgetting something this important for so long
is making me think that something is wrong.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:00.580
Good point.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:04.210
She seems in good shape when she's at home,
but only ever talks about random stuff.

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:08.000
And yesterday she was stuck in waitress mode
even after coming home.

00:13:08.250 --> 00:13:09.040
Clickety-clack!

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:10.460
Hey, Shamiko, do you have a minute?

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:13.630
Uh, Shamiko? You okay?

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:15.000
Oh! A customer!

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.830
What would you like to order, ma'am?

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:19.670
I'd like some lemon tea
with a slice of lemon cake, please.

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:21.540
I'll have that out right away.

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:25.960
It went back and forth like that until somehow we
ended up playing pretend classy café for about an hour.

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:27.290
Why did you play along...?

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:31.000
Actually, I tried to enter
Shamiko's consciousness yesterday.

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:34.040
But everything was so fuzzy
I couldn't even find the entrance.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:38.830
Either she's not getting good sleep or she's been
put under the influence of something at work.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.380
Like a spell or hypnotic suggestion.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:44.580
Unless we do something, Shamiko's gonna end up
being the star attraction of that shop!

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:48.210
We know for a fact there are demons at Café Asura.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:51.750
All of our prep is done.
So let's just force our way through the barrier!

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.920
It's time to launch operation:
Absolutely No Employment For Shamiko!

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:55.790
<b>YEAH!</b>

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:56.040
YEAH!

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:58.670
Uh, I think our plan is gonna need
a more positive name than that!

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:02.330
I remember this!

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:06.210
This is one of those temporary vessels
that woman with the glasses made!

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.630
<b>HEH</b>

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.630
<b>HEH</b>

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:06.630
<b>HEH</b>

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:06.630
Mwa hah ha

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:08.460
Look! I can move around!

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:17.250
<b>LOVELY~</b>

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:10.670
You're so adorable, Ancestor!

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:14.540
Fill me in, Momo. What are we doing in this park?

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:17.830
This is in the total opposite direction of Café Asura!

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:21.330
What? You didn't explain anything to her, Momo?

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:24.080
Huff! Huff! Huff! Huff! Huff! Huff!

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:22.130
Nope.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:24.080
Whatever. Let's get started!

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:25.210
Huh? What?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.250
Whoa!

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:51.540
Here's the deal. We're going to have
Mikan shoot at Asura's barrier.

00:14:52.210 --> 00:14:55.210
My main offensive speciality is long-range attacks!

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:56.330
Oh yeah?

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.210
I get too nervous up close and can't land any hits.

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:01.790
But my accuracy from super-long distances
is pretty solid.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:03.670
That's the opposite of how it should be...

00:15:07.290 --> 00:15:08.540
I found it!

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:11.130
The barrier is just to the right of Asura's main entrance!

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:13.920
You can see it from way over here?!
It's over a kilometer away!

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:15.630
Well, I can't see it with my eyes.

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:19.880
But this high hill that we're standing on
is actually the source of the city's leylines.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.580
As long as I know the general location of the building,

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:24.290
I can trace the leylines
and use them to determine the location.

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:26.000
It's the perfect spot for a magical sniper.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:27.420
Ms. Lilith. Here, hold on this.

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:29.380
Huh? What is this thing?

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:33.790
If you just scrub the barrier with that wand,
then we'll be able to overwrite part of it.

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:31.330
<b>SHAKE</b>

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:31.330
<b>SHAKE</b>

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.330
<b>SHAKE</b>

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.330
<b>SHAKE</b>

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:35.540
That's the gist of our plan, so now...

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:40.210
...we're going to have you ride on Mikan's arrow and
send you flying straight to the doorstep of Café Asura!

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:40.790
What?!

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.040
I'm going to fly? Fly to the café?!

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.460
Why didn't I get the memo!

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.170
Because you wouldn't have come if you had, right?

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:47.750
You're darn right I wouldn't!

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:52.250
Besides, if this wand is enough to overwrite the barrier,
why didn't you just have Shamiko take it?!

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:55.420
A counterattack gets triggered
if an outsider tries to mess with the barrier.

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:58.460
But it takes several seconds for that attack to hit
once you enter the sphere of influence.

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:02.830
So our only option is to charge in at high-speed
and overwrite the barrier immediately.

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:06.250
There's roughly a distance of 1 kilometer
between here and Café Asura.

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:07.960
I can have you there in one second flat.

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:12.080
So what you're saying is, you're about to send me flying
at the ridiculous speed of 1 kilometer per second.

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:14.500
Yeah, but we're not asking you to do it for free.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.130
I'll give you these "create a vessel anytime" tickets.

00:16:15.460 --> 00:16:19.830
<b>VESSEL</b>

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:19.170
You couldn't make them look any better
than a cheap "shoulder massage" ticket?!

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:21.040
Fine! I'm in! I'll do this thing!

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:25.000
But there's only a few seconds
of leeway after I land, right?

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.580
What happens if Mikan or I fail to pull this off?

00:16:27.580 --> 00:16:28.250
Not a problem.

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:31.250
I've got 10 doll bodies here that you can use.

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:33.210
We can keep going as long as you have spare lives.

00:16:33.210 --> 00:16:33.380
CLUMP...

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:34.380
Spare what...?

00:16:34.790 --> 00:16:37.960
All right. Time to start operation: Retake Shamiko!

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:39.210
Did you say "spare lives"?!

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:44.420
<b>ANCESTOR</b>

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:42.290
It's okay. We can fail up to 10 times.

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:42.790
Oh, God...

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:44.330
Relax, I won't fail!

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:48.290
Hey, Yuko. Yuko?

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.880
Ah! I'm sorry! I was spacing out.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:52.130
You feelin' tired?

00:16:52.710 --> 00:16:54.920
Sounds like you need to take a break, Yuko.

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:56.670
Head to the back and treat yourself to some food.

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:00.630
So, Yuko, hun? I'm wondering if maybe...

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:00.630
<b>SMASH!!</b>

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:02.250
Huh?

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.080
An arrow? Uh, what on Earth?

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:07.670
Boss! It's an arrowgram!

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:10.380
I've never gotten one before! How delightful!

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:18.080
<b>I'LL SHOOT IF YOU RUN</b>

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:18.080
<b>LET'S HANDLE THINGS PEACEFULLY</b>

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:18.080
<b>SORRY ABOUT THIS</b>

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:18.080
<b>HINATSUKI</b>

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:13.170
I'll shoot if you run! Let's handle things peacefully.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:15.130
Sorry about this. Hinatsuki.

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:16.540
It's the exact opposite of delightful!

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:18.080
<b>Heartbeat</b>

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:18.080
<b>Thampir-Thampir</b>

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:18.460
In fact, it sounds very much like a threat!

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:21.580
And it seems that something
has tampered with Lady Sakura's barrier!

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:24.000
Well shucks, it must be the work of a priestess.

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:26.170
They're called "magical girls" these days.

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:29.460
Let's do this, I haven't dropped
a living priestess down the pit latrine in forever!

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:32.000
Uh, Lico?! Did you not read the part about "peaceful"?!

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.080
Also, this town doesn't have a pit latrine!

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:56.330
<b>SECONDS</b>

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.290
Pardon the interruption.

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:03.250
One human and one familiar here. Mind if we come in?

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:04.330
A magical girl!

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:07.790
That's an awfully elaborate outfit
that you've got on, missy.

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:11.040
Sorry to say, but all we're serving
is rocks for you to kick. Is that okay?

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:12.290
Uh, Lico?!

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:14.000
Is Yuko Yoshida here?

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:18.040
We're not a maid café
where you can just pick your favorite girl.

00:18:18.170 --> 00:18:19.330
Yuko Yoshida!

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:20.580
We're pulling out of here!

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:22.790
Hold on, that room's only for staff!

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.290
Huh? Oh, it's Momo. Um...

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.540
Did you come to visit as a customer?

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:30.580
Come on, you're forgetting something really important!

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:32.420
"Something important"...?

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.330
What could that be?

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:37.210
Is there something wrong with the food?

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:39.210
No, this food is really yummy!

00:18:39.210 --> 00:18:40.750
That's not what I meant.

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:43.290
Yuko was supposed to come here as our negotiator.

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:47.380
I don't appreciate you brainwashing her,
and then exploiting her for manual labor like this!

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:49.380
She's clearly not in good health right now!

00:18:49.380 --> 00:18:51.080
Shamiko! Snap out of it!

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:53.250
"Brainwashing"?

00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:54.500
Stay right there, Lico.

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:57.250
I'm the owner of this place, so let me do the talking.

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:00.880
<b>DOOM</b>

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:00.880
<b>DOOM</b>

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:00.880
<b>DOOM</b>

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:00.880
<b>DOOM</b>

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:00.880
<b>DOOM</b>

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:00.880
<b>DOOM</b>

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:00.040
Just to be clear, I'm quite strong.

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:00.710
Huh?

00:19:00.880 --> 00:19:05.580
On top of being a non-combatant,
our owner is aggravatingly weak and injured,

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:09.130
but he's still trying to protect us by bluffing hard enough
to get some leverage in the negotiations.

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:10.500
Color me impressed.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:11.380
Shush, Lico!

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:14.040
Don't just blurt out my actual power level like that!

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:16.420
You're supposed to roll with the idea
that I'm super strong!

00:19:16.540 --> 00:19:17.580
Alrighty.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:20.080
Uh, I can hear everything you're saying...

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:24.290
Snore.... snore...

00:19:21.830 --> 00:19:24.290
Shamiko? Earth to Shamiko.

00:19:24.290 --> 00:19:26.540
It's time to wake up, Shamiko!

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:30.250
Listen, Lico is a Huli jing fox
who has lived for a pretty long time

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:34.250
and always takes great care
to make meals that are meant to soothe the soul.

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:37.290
It's true that her food can temporarily
make someone forget about

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:38.920
the daily stress and exhaustion they deal with.

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:43.080
However, the effect is no different from ordinary dishes
with deep flavors like garlic ramen.

00:19:43.420 --> 00:19:48.710
But more to the point, even if you assume that Lico's food
really did make her forget something important...

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:49.460
JAB!

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:52.960
...that means whatever you asked
this poor girl to do was stressing her out!

00:19:57.040 --> 00:19:57.750
JAB!

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:01.000
The fact you're speechless means
I'm right on the money! Eh, Magical Girl?

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:03.830
Surely you must agree, Ms. Familiar?

00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:06.830
Don't drag me into it! I have no spare lives left!

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.460
Also, I'm not a familiar!

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:10.830
I would very much like for Yuko to work here!

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:14.830
Tell me, are you even offering her proper compensation
for the work you have her do?

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:16.420
Compensation...?

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:17.500
Yeah, what he said!

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:20.420
The food that we make here is truly good for you.

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:22.250
Although, if you eat 10 times more than usual

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:24.630
it's possible to get stuck on a high
and suffer from light amnesia.

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:25.380
WHAT?!

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:25.500
<b>CLANK</b>

00:20:25.420 --> 00:20:29.080
But even then, all it takes is a single day
to make a complete recovery.

00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:30.580
Ten times...?

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:33.580
So if you eat ten times the norm you forget things?

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.540
Yep. In particularly effective cases.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:39.500
Lico, dear! Why am I just hearing about this now?!

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:42.790
Let's see. Probably because
this is the first time I've ever told anybody.

00:20:42.790 --> 00:20:44.040
LICO!!

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:50.750
Snore... snore...

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:51.630
Our girl here was eating mountains of the leftover food
that you were sending her home with.

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:54.880
She kept going on about how she felt sorry
for the sandwiches and stuff.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:56.880
<b>WHEW</b>

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:56.880
The owner gave me all these.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:01.880
That means she wasn't sleeping well and spacing out
due to the high she was getting from all the food.

00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:02.830
Sleep deprivation, basically.

00:21:03.420 --> 00:21:09.170
If she eats regular food for a day and then sleeps it off,
I think she should remember what she forgot.

00:21:09.170 --> 00:21:10.000
GROVEL!

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:12.330
You have my sincere and honest apologies
for all the problems we've caused!

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:11.040
<b>GROVEL!!</b>

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:11.830
<b>PLOP</b>

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:14.130
There's no need for you to grovel...

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.330
I mean, I did break your window.

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:20.880
And you mentioned something about negotiations?

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:21.710
Not now.

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:25.880
My priority is getting Yuko home for some rest.
We'll be taking our leave for today.

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:28.080
Oh, I see...

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:35.710
Onward!

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:38.960
Yeah, that's right. We're gonna call it quits for now.

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:40.460
Onward! Onward!

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:47.790
So... did I forget something important or what?

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:49.630
Don't worry about it right now.

00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:50.880
Onward! Onward!

00:21:50.130 --> 00:21:52.880
The reality is that I was
putting you under too much pressure.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:53.540
Onwar-

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:57.750
No... I want to remember.

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:02.290
Right now... my very top priority is...

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:04.500
Uhh....

00:22:07.130 --> 00:22:12.290
That's right! My mission is to put
a big, fat smile on Momo's face!

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:14.960
Wrong!

00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:16.670
You're totally wrong!

00:22:16.670 --> 00:22:20.330
Momo, take it easy! I don't have any spare lives left!

00:22:20.330 --> 00:22:25.420
Don't give up, Shamiko! Go home for now and...
get some well-deserved rest.

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:46.790
We met again. It's drama?

00:22:46.790 --> 00:22:49.790
I'll go tell someone at once

00:22:49.960 --> 00:22:52.710
As soon as possible

00:22:52.830 --> 00:22:55.330
Oh, even the post box says "Good morning"

00:22:55.330 --> 00:22:57.540
Even my tail is sharp

00:22:57.540 --> 00:23:01.380
If our usual members gather and jump over the white lines

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:04.130
Today will start, too

00:23:04.290 --> 00:23:07.920
A sudden mystery

00:23:08.040 --> 00:23:11.290
Makes me feel dizzy and at a loss

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:15.830
But we will hold hands and go anywhere we want

00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:22.750
The city is turning and shining

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:25.670
Around and around many times

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:28.380
The night mixed with dreams

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:31.330
Will make you blossom

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:34.250
The tetragon that surrounds four sides

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:37.130
Ah, a bouquet for our neighborhood

00:23:37.130 --> 00:23:40.080
Hey, now, just a little bit more

00:23:40.330 --> 00:23:44.130
Show me the flowers secretly

00:23:44.330 --> 00:23:47.790
Once more if I get greedy!

00:23:56.170 --> 00:24:11.080
<b>PREVIEW</b>

00:23:57.210 --> 00:24:00.420
Thanks to the demon café owner who lives in town,
along with the help of Lico and Ryo,

00:24:00.420 --> 00:24:02.960
I've started to figure out a lot of things
that I didn't understand before!

00:24:03.130 --> 00:24:04.920
Like the reason Momo loves Miss Tama Sakura so much.

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.170
Shamiko, you need to remember

00:24:06.170 --> 00:24:07.210
what happened 10 years ago!

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:11.080
<b>RAID! THE PINK PLAN TO RETAKE SHAMIKO!</b>

00:24:07.210 --> 00:24:09.080
Now is the time to put those succubus powers to use!

00:24:09.080 --> 00:24:10.920
Sour things are good for your brain, you know!
